  "damageType": "",
  "resolution": "attack",
  "saveAbility": "",
  "fullText": "Wreathing your limb in Ki, you form the visage of a cutting edge - one more potent than a standard blade of its size. For the duration of this Technique your chosen limb is treated as a Melee Weapon known as a Ki Edge with the following statistics: You are Proficient with the Ki Edge. The Ki Edge counts as a Finesse Simple Melee Weapon. You may also choose to apply either the Nick or Vex Weapon Mastery Property to it whenever you cast this Technique. The chosen Weapon Mastery Property is known to you when used with this Weapon. Attack Rolls and Techniques with the Ki Edge can use your Omni Attack Roll and Omni Save DC. The Ki Edge deals 1d6 Energy Damage, you may also use either your Armed Technique Casting Modifier or Omni Technique Casting Modifier as the Damage Modifier. Armed Techniques using the Ki Edge can be treated as Ki Techniques for the sake of the Energy Clash Snap Decision. You can not be disarmed of the Ki Edge. It cannot be Thrown, nor can it be used for any Technique that would require it leaving your hand. This Technique cannot benefit from any Mastery Options."
