  "resolution": "save",
  "saveAbility": "Strength",
  "fullText": "You tap into the elemental energies of the planet to reshape the terrain or manipulate the weather, depending on your needs. You may take one of the following Actions per casting of this Technique:\nRaise Terrain (Wall). As an Action, you cause the ground to rise and form a wall of solid earth, rock, or other natural material at a location within Range. The wall extends from that location in a direction of your choice with dimensions of up to 30ft long, 10ft high, and 5ft thick. The wall has HP equal to (15x the Technique's Ki Rank) and an AC equal to your Omni Save DC. The wall crumbles at the end of the duration, when you create a new one, or when it is dispelled or destroyed earlier. As a Bonus Action while within Range of the wall, you can reshape it. You may alter the direction it extends in or the dimensions (as long as the total volume doesn't change).\nManipulate Weather (Storm). As a Bonus Action, you can alter the weather to create a storm with conditions such as gusting winds, heavy rain, or dark clouds. The storm covers a 60ft radius Emanation around you.\nHeavy Rain. Extinguishes open flames and imposes Disadvantage on Perception Checks relying on sight.\nStrong Winds. Creatures flying in this area must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw or be Launched 10ft away from the center of the storm. This effect is repeated each turn they begin within the storm.\nAlternatively, you can pay an extra 3 Ki in Upkeep and expend the required Action Economy for each effect to maintain both effects simultaneously.\nAt Higher Ranks: For each Rank above the original that this Technique is cast, the attributes change as follows:\nRank 3 (12 Ki): Allied creatures within a storm or wall created by this Technique may expend their Reaction upon the initial casting to take the Hide Action.\nRank 4 (15 Ki): Enemy creatures treat the storm as Difficult Terrain and the wall gains Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, Slashing, and Energy Damage."
